    "What is your relationship with mathematics?": "Mathematics has always been a challenging subject for me, but I appreciate its logical structure. While it's not my strongest skill, I enjoy problem-solving and seeing how equations can model real-world scenarios. My background in computer science helps me connect math to practical applications, even if abstract concepts sometimes feel overwhelming.",
    "Do you ever get anxious when thinking about mathematics?": "Yes, especially with complex topics like calculus or advanced algebra. The pressure to understand proofs or solve intricate problems can be stressful, but I’ve learned to break them down into smaller, more manageable steps. My anxiety is moderate—it motivates me to work harder rather than paralyzing me.",
    "Did you ever use AI to support your math learning in the last year? If yes, how was your experience?": "I used an AI tutoring tool for practicing algebra and calculus problems. It was helpful for immediate feedback, but I preferred working through examples myself afterward to solidify my understanding. The explanations were clear, though sometimes too technical for my level.",
